site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?u=8069d9b7bc6ab503ce83dfcfa53fd021672aeccf&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"I think I did, in fact, make an oopsie. I did not make this clearer\r\n\r\n> Unless there's a misunderstanding, and changing height also affects radius, similarly.\r\n\r\nBecause indeed, both properties do affect each other. Therefore, to reduce maintenance and localization burden, ideally it would be nice if this was summarized in the leading description.\r\n\r\nHowever, I **do see** a benefit in mentioning this behaviour on the properties themselves: It's much nicer to visualize on the spot. This is good, I think.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101732#pullrequestreview-2945908268","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101732","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-06-20T12:25:28Z"}]